<li about="#cite_note-93" id="cite_note-93" data-mw-footnote-number="92"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCnU"><a href="#cite_ref-93" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCnY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCnc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-93" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt375" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwCng" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Croucher"},"first":{"wt":"Martin"},"title":{"wt":"Myth of &apos;Babu Sassi&apos; Remains After Burj Cranes Come Down"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.khaleejtimes.com/displayarticle.asp?xfile=data/theuae/2009/November/theuae_November338.xml&amp;section=theuae&amp;col="},"access-date":{"wt":"3 June 2011"},"newspaper":{"wt":"[[Khaleej Times]]"},"date":{"wt":"11 November 2009"},"archive-date":{"wt":"1 October 2012"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20121001080528/http://www.khaleejtimes.com/displayarticle.asp?xfile=data%2Ftheuae%2F2009%2FNovember%2Ftheuae_November338.xml&amp;section=theuae&amp;col="},"url-status":{"wt":"dead"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFCroucher2009" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt375">Croucher, Martin (11 November 2009). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20121001080528/http://www.khaleejtimes.com/displayarticle.asp?xfile=data%2Ftheuae%2F2009%2FNovember%2Ftheuae_November338.xml&amp;section=theuae&amp;col=" class="external text" id="mwCnk">"Myth of 'Babu Sassi' Remains After Burj Cranes Come Down"</a>. <i id="mwCno"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khaleej_Times" title="Khaleej Times" id="mwCns">Khaleej Times</a></i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.khaleejtimes.com/displayarticle.asp?xfile=data/theuae/2009/November/theuae_November338.xml&amp;section=theuae&amp;col=" class="external text" id="mwCnw">the original</a> on 1 October 2012<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwCn0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwCn4">3 June</span> 2011</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Khaleej+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Myth+of+%27Babu+Sassi%27+Remains+After+Burj+Cranes+Come+Down&amp;rft.date=2009-11-11&amp;rft.aulast=Croucher&amp;rft.aufirst=Martin&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.khaleejtimes.com%2Fdisplayarticle.asp%3Fxfile%3Ddata%2Ftheuae%2F2009%2FNovember%2Ftheuae_November338.xml%26section%3Dtheuae%26col%3D&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ABurj+Khalifa" class="Z3988" about="#mwt375" id="mwCn8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-GeoMarc-94" id="cite_note-GeoMarc-94" data-mw-footnote-number="93"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCoA"><a href="#cite_ref-GeoMarc_94-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCoE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCoI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-GeoMarc-94" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt652" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwCoM" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFHarry_G._Poulos,_Grahame_Bunce2008" class="citation news cs1">Harry G. Poulos, Grahame Bunce (2008). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110409115002/http://www.geomarc.it/Poulos_%26_Bunce_2008.pdf" class="external text" id="mwCoQ">"Foundation Design for the Burj Dubai – The World's Tallest Building"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwCoU">(PDF)</span>. 6th International Conference on Case Histories in Geotechnical Engineering. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.geomarc.it/Poulos_&amp;_Bunce_2008.pdf" class="external text" id="mwCoY">the original</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwCoc">(PDF)</span> on 9 April 2011<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwCog">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwCok">24 September</span> 2016</span>. <q id="mwCoo">Medium dense to very loose granular silty sands (Marine Deposits) are underlain by successions of very weak to weak sandstone interbedded with very weakly cemented sand, gypsiferous fine-grained sandstone/siltstone, and weak to moderately weak conglomerate/calcisiltite.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Foundation+Design+for+the+Burj+Dubai+%E2%80%93+The+World%27s+Tallest+Building&amp;rft.date=2008&amp;rft.au=Harry+G.+Poulos%2C+Grahame+Bunce&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.geomarc.it%2FPoulos_%26_Bunce_2008.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ABurj+Khalifa" class="Z3988" id="mwCos"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-95" id="cite_note-95" data-mw-footnote-number="94"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCow"><a href="#cite_ref-95" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCo0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCo4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-95" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt380" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwCo8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"Burj Khalifa {{!}} PDF {{!}} Engineering {{!}} Civil Engineering"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.scribd.com/presentation/403504617/Burj-Khalifa"},"access-date":{"wt":"2024-07-09"},"website":{"wt":"Scribd"},"language":{"wt":"en"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt380" id="mwCpA"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.scribd.com/presentation/403504617/Burj-Khalifa" class="external text" id="mwCpE">"Burj Khalifa | PDF | Engineering | Civil Engineering"</a>. <i id="mwCpI">Scribd</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwCpM">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwCpQ">9 July</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Scribd&amp;rft.atitle=Burj+Khalifa+%7C+PDF+%7C+Engineering+%7C+Civil+Engineering&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.scribd.com%2Fpresentation%2F403504617%2FBurj-Khalifa&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ABurj+Khalifa" class="Z3988" about="#mwt380" id="mwCpU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-GeoPrac2010-01-04-96" id="cite_note-GeoPrac2010-01-04-96" data-mw-footnote-number="95"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCpY"><a href="#cite_ref-GeoPrac2010-01-04_96-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCpc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCpg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-GeoPrac2010-01-04-96" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt657" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwCpk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFRandy_Post2010" class="citation news cs1">Randy Post (4 January 2010). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.geoprac.net/geonews-mainmenu-63/64-project-related/634-foundations-for-the-burj-dubai-worlds-tallest-building" class="external text" id="mwCpo">"Foundations and Geotechnical Engineering for the Burj Dubai – World's Tallest Building"</a>. GeoPrac. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20160923032346/http://www.geoprac.net/geonews-mainmenu-63/64-project-related/634-foundations-for-the-burj-dubai-worlds-tallest-building" class="external text" id="mwCps">Archived</a> from the original on 23 September 2016<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwCpw">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwCp0">24 September</span> 2016</span>. <q id="mwCp4">The soil/rock conditions were generally loose to medium dense sands overlying weak to very weak sandstone and siltstone with interbeds of gypsiferous and carbonate cemented layers (still relatively weak).</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Foundations+and+Geotechnical+Engineering+for+the+Burj+Dubai+%E2%80%93+World%27s+Tallest+Building&amp;rft.date=2010-01-04&amp;rft.au=Randy+Post&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.geoprac.net%2Fgeonews-mainmenu-63%2F64-project-related%2F634-foundations-for-the-burj-dubai-worlds-tallest-building&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ABurj+Khalifa" class="Z3988" id="mwCp8"></span></span></li>
